paper_type:
- screening (boolean): true if the paper describes any sort of screen against a protein target. False if the paper does not describe a chemical screen.
- known (boolean): True if the paper describes starting from a previously identified or reported drug, lead compound, or hit. False if the paper uses a screening technique, as defined below, in order to find the compound of interest discussed in the abstract.
screens:
- fragment (boolean): true if the paper describes testing fragment-sized molecules against a protein target to find ligands, using techniques such as NMR, X-ray crystallography, or biophysical assays. Virtual screening of fragments is excluded from this category. False if the paper does not describe a fragment screen.
- Undirected (boolean): true if the paper describes testing a real-world library of molecules against a protein target to find ligands, using high-throughput plate-based biophysical assays. Screening of fragment-sized molecules is excluded from this category. False if the paper does not describe screening a real-world collection of molecules.
- directed (boolean): false in all cases. This field is a temporary placeholder.
- virtual (boolean): true if the paper describes using virtual screening techniques to identify ligands binding a protein target, using techniques such as structure-based docking or ligand-based molecular similarity. False if the paper does not describe the use of virtual screening methods.
- del (boolean): true if the paper describes testing a DNA-encoded library of molecules (sometimes referred to as a DEL) against a protein target to find ligands. False if the paper does not describe a DEL screen.

